What is a Military Powered Exoskeleton?
Military powered exoskeletons are wearable robotic systems designed to enhance soldiers' physical capabilities through advanced actuator technology and artificial intelligence. These cutting-edge systems integrate hydraulic/pneumatic actuators, advanced control systems, and power units to provide strength amplification, endurance enhancement, and mobility improvement. Modern military exoskeletons can enable soldiers to carry heavy loads (up to 200 lbs) with reduced fatigue, traverse difficult terrain efficiently, and integrate with existing combat systems.
